        "original_id": "d2349e30-84f5-5c36-96f4-5bfdb7d8d90c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Companies: Dain Rauscher Wessels, Berenberg Bank, Royal Bank of Canada\n- People: John G. Taft, Johann Berenberg, Paul Berenberg, the Berenberg family\n- Places: Minneapolis, Minnesota, Hamburg\n- Topics: brokerage, investment banking, private banking, acquisitions, company origins\n\nFacts:\n- Berenberg Bank was founded in Hamburg in 1590 by the Belgian-origined Berenberg family.\n- Johann Berenberg became a co-owner of Berenberg Bank in 1748 together with his brother Paul Berenberg.\n- After Paul Berenberg died in 1768, Johann Berenberg became the sole owner of Berenberg Bank.\n- Dain Rauscher Wessels traced its origins to several smaller regional securities firms founded in the 1920s and 1930s.\n- Dain Rauscher Wessels was a brokerage and investment banking firm based in Minneapolis, Minnesota.\n- Royal Bank of Canada acquired Dain Rauscher in 2001.\n- John G. Taft's unit at Dougherty was later acquired by Dain Rauscher.\n- John G. Taft began working with Royal Bank of Canada after Royal Bank of Canada acquired Dain Rauscher in 2001.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "ec8c23a7-403c-54d9-b85f-b6cf85f7e180",
        "text": "Page: Dain Rauscher Wessels. Sentence: Dain Rauscher Wessels was a brokerage and investment banking firm based in Minneapolis, Minnesota.\nPage: Dain Rauscher Wessels. Sentence: The firm traced its origins to a number of smaller regional securities firms founded in the 1920s and 1930s.\nPage: Berenberg Bank. Sentence: KG, commonly known as Berenberg Bank, is a Hamburg-based multinational investment banking and private banking company, founded by the Belgian-origined Berenberg family in 1590.\nPage: John G. Taft. Sentence: His unit at Dougherty was later acquired by Dain Rauscher, and Taft began working with Royal Bank of Canada (RBC) when it acquired Dain Rauscher in 2001.\nPage: Johann Berenberg. Sentence: He was a co-owner of Berenberg Bank from 1748, with his brother, senator Paul Berenberg, and after the latter's death in 1768 the sole owner.",
